  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The five seats",
      "items": [
        "FORGE - build and sequence (qwen3.7-plus, Alibaba coding plan)",
        "FINISHER - verify, gate, approve risky commands (claude-sonnet-5)",
        "RECON - cited, confidence-graded evidence (deepseek-v4-pro)",
        "SPARRING - attack plans and dissent (hermes-4-405b)",
        "ENVOY - outbound tone pass (qwen3.7-flash)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Deliberation protocol",
      "items": [
        "Independent drafts, then anonymized cross-examination, then weighted synthesis",
        "Dissent is preserved as a Minority Report",
        "Uncited position flips are logged as conformity",
        "Agreement is detected by Jaccard overlap, not by vote"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Why it stays honest",
      "items": [
        "Ledger weights move only when a run is settled against reality",
        "Laplace-smoothed per seat x domain, 45-day half-life",
        "CRITICAL commands have no override; HIGH needs a different model family or the operator",
        "Raising a spend ceiling needs a two-person token; lowering is free"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Cost posture",
      "items": [
        "Idle cost is zero \u2014 councils, cron ticks, and kanban dispatch are all event-driven",
        "Transport is stdlib urllib and subprocess; no httpx or requests"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Casting constraints",
      "items": [
        "Four model families on purpose - same-family seats agree too easily",
        "SPARRING is provisioned with every toolset stripped: it argues, it never touches the filesystem",
        "FORGE routes through an Alibaba coding plan; the other four go via OpenRouter",
        "models.py checks the OpenRouter catalog for candidate freshness on a 24h cache",
        "Quick pair is FORGE + FINISHER; full council adds RECON + SPARRING"
      ]
    }
  ]
